# Alembic migration safety

Set `DATABASE_URL` explicitly for every migration command. Temporary SQLite
tests may use a file under `tempfile.gettempdir()`. The protected repository
file `agencyforge.db` and every symlink resolving to it are refused. Other
persistent targets need `ALLOW_NON_TMP_MIGRATIONS=1` after an operator has
verified the target and backup.

For an old SQLite database, create and verify a separate backup first, then use
`python -m database.adopt_legacy --backup /safe/agencyforge-legacy-backup.sqlite
--target /tmp/agencyforge-legacy-import.sqlite`. The adoption tool copies the
backup, verifies the baseline schema before stamping, upgrades to `head`, runs
`alembic check`, and compares application row counts. See the README for the
full recovery procedure. Never stamp or upgrade the protected database.

Legacy SQLite baseline adoption is distinct from moving SQLite records to
PostgreSQL. The application does not implement a SQLite-to-PostgreSQL transfer.
